hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18659","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Wail from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to trade in measures in Madinah, and we called ourselves brokers, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us and named us with a name better than what we called ourselves, and he said: O company of merchants, this sale is attended by idle talk and oaths, so mix it with charity."
